{"t": 1793860739.3498154, "event_type": "chat.tool_result", "session_id": "03-build-from-request", "tool_call_id": "exec-cde50ac3-cf4b-4ea5-a2a9-352d21897d25", "tool_name": "cc.cc_material", "result": "{\"status\": \"completed\", \"result\": {\"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"{\\n  \\\"cc\\\": \\\"demo.methodology\\\",\\n  \\\"material\\\": \\\"method\\\",\\n  \\\"media_type\\\": \\\"text/markdown\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Agent workflow for evaluating the synthetic served compute demo.\\\",\\n  \\\"truncated\\\": false,\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"# Synthetic compute evaluation method\\\\n\\\\n1. Use cc_list and cc_describe to discover the demo CCs and their ports,\\\\n   materials, required resources, and declared effects. Read this method and limits.\\\\n2. Ensure demo.compute_service was built with build_image.py and its image ID\\\\n   identifies the built application. Ask the host to grant declared effects.\\\\n3. Start demo.compute_service capability api with a stable operation key.\\\\n   Require state running and readiness ready; retain the instance identifier.\\\\n4. Pass the returned host-issued environment handle to\\\\n   demo.service_client capability benchmark as engine, with a workload such as\\\\n   {\\\\\\\"points\\\\\\\": [0, 1, 3]}. If the host API returns endpoints rather than a handle,\\\\n   have the host register an environment resource with the api URL and instance\\\\n   identifier, then use that host-issued resource handle. Do not invent a handle.\\\\n5. Inspect the assigned workspace with demo.workspace_inspect capability inspect,\\\\n   using its workspace handle. Retain summary.json and series.json artifacts.\\\\n6. Stop the service instance in a finally/cleanup step, including after failures.\\\\n   Inspect the stop result and confirm state stopped before claiming cleanup.\\\\n\\\\nThe service shows HTTP lifecycle and synthetic multiplication correctness.\\\\nRuntime metadata describes the service's OS and Python; it is not attestation.\\\\nClient metrics describe loopback HTTP requests including Python client overhead.\\\\nWorkspace results describe bounded file inventory and simple structural metadata.\\\\nNone of these establish model quality, inference TTFT, token throughput, or\\\\nproduction performance. Empty results may be valid successful observations.\\\\n\\\\nNever report success when a receipt is failed, blocked, or unknown. Partial\\\\nreceipts retain observations but do not establish workload completion. Report the\\\\nfailure and evidence limits. Retry an identical operation with the same key;\\\\ndo not change inputs or grants under that key. If effects are denied, a host\\\\ngrant is required; obtain authorization and use a new key for a changed request.\\\\nAn unknown execution needs host reconciliation before a fresh execution.\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"authority\\\": \\\"Reading this grants no execution authority.\\\"\\n}\"}], \"structuredContent\": null, \"_meta\": null}, \"error\": null}"}
{"t": 1793860739.352839, "event_type": "chat.tool_call", "session_id": "03-build-from-request", "tool_call": {"tool_call_id": "exec-3d1f8739-97c9-4852-84c6-5101fa2e88f4", "name": "cc.cc_material", "arguments": {"cc": "demo.methodology", "material": "limits"}}}
{"t": 1793860739.3710222, "event_type": "chat.tool_result", "session_id": "03-build-from-request", "tool_call_id": "exec-3d1f8739-97c9-4852-84c6-5101fa2e88f4", "tool_name": "cc.cc_material", "result": "{\"status\": \"completed\", \"result\": {\"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"{\\n  \\\"cc\\\": \\\"demo.methodology\\\",\\n  \\\"material\\\": \\\"limits\\\",\\n  \\\"media_type\\\": \\\"text/markdown\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Interpretation and evidence limits.\\\",\\n  \\\"truncated\\\": false,\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"# Evidence limits\\\\n\\\\n- This demo multiplies numbers by two; it performs no inference.\\\\n- Synthetic loopback client timings are NOT inference-engine TTFT or token-rate\\\\n  evidence. They include transport, scheduling, JSON parsing, and client overhead.\\\\n- p50/p95 use nearest-rank percentiles of successful requests only. Empty workloads\\\\n  succeed with count zero, an empty series, and null percentile/runtime values.\\\\n- Failed requests yield partial results, possibly with zero successful requests.\\\\n- A ready endpoint confirms HTTP startup only, not scientific validity or quality.\\\\n- The image pins an OS/Python base; build_image.py must bind the built application\\\\n  ID. Base-image identity alone does not identify this service implementation.\\\\n- Published Docker bridge ports cannot enforce no-egress. The image service\\\\n  therefore declares network.request along with process.exec and network.listen.\\\\n- Runtime metadata is self-reported; no hardware or remote identity is attested.\\\\n- Workspace inventories skip dependency/cache directories and symbolic links.\\\\n  Counts cover at most max_files ordinary files (default 2000).\\\\n- Structured metadata covers at most 50 eligible files, each at most 1 MiB.\\\\n  Parser errors and missing optional YAML support are recorded per file.\\\\n- No contents are written into the inspected workspace. Retained artifacts live\\\\n  in host-managed output storage. Inventory metadata can still be sensitive.\\\\n- Passive methodology materials execute nothing. A request CC is a design input,\\\\n  never an implemented executable package.\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"authority\\\": \\\"Reading this grants no execution authority.\\\"\\n}\"}], \"structuredContent\": null, \"_meta\": null}, \"error\": null}"}
